ices of the people.\n\nCharters and Constitutions\nThe fourth Law Element of most major societies and empires since the beginning of human civilization is Charters and Constitutions being the mandates and instruments of authority to govern by the leaders of a society and its people.\n\nCodes and Statutes\nThe fifth Law Element of most major societies and empires since the beginning of human civilization is Codes and Statutes being the key categories of rules for the proper administration of the state, its branches and the various organisations and entities that operate within the society and between other societies.\n\nCases and Judgements\nThe sixth Law Element of most major societies is Cases and Judgements being the cumulative judgements and knowledge of jurists in the protection and operation of the law.\n\nTreaties and Concords\nThe seventh Law Element of most major societies is Treaties and Concords being the agreements between societies to unite under common forms of law and regulations.\n\nRegulations and Policies\nThe eighth Law Element of most major societies is Regulations and Policies being the rules of administration by the departments and agencies of government.\n\nRegisters, Rolls and Records\nThe ninth Law Element of most major societies is the Registers, Rolls and Records being the official registers and records of the society, especially in the administration of rights and property.",
